tomer service to constituents including our off-campus locations. Qualifications Summary Bachelor's degree preferred or equivalent work experience. Ability to meet deadlines, detail-oriented, organizational ability, and uphold policy. Knowledge of and experience with office productivity tools, including word processing and spreadsheet packages. Experience with Ellucian Banner and Degree Works highly valued. Customer service skills and a caring attitude. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top ACADEMY GENERAL - Substitute Teacher I Job Classification Hourly Under Half (<20) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2021-10-26 Applications Taken Until 2024-05-31 Position Summary Looking for mature adults who can supervise high-school students during study halls and when a regular teacher must be out. Qualifications Summary Must be able to follow lesson plans left and have some classroom management skills to maintain classroom order. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top ACADEMY GENERAL - Admin Asst Academy Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-04-29 Position Summary Andrews Academy (AA) is seeking an Administrative Assistant who will serve as a key support professional in the daily operations of the school. This individual is responsible for maintaining efficient office operations, facilitating communication among students, parents, faculty, and staff, and supporting administrative functions. As a first point of contact, the Administrative Assistant represents the school with professionalism, warmth, and a commitment to the mission: “Think deeply, live fully, serve unselfishly, trust God completely.” Qualifications Summary High school diploma required; college coursework preferred Previous office or administrative experience required Demonstrated proficiency in office productivity tools (word processing, spreadsheets, email, scheduling systems) Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top AIRPARK OPERATIONS - Flight Instructor Job Classification Hourly Under Half (<20) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2019-05-31 Position Summary Under general direction of the Chief Flight Instructor, conducts quality flight instruction required in the professional pilot programs at Andrews University. Note: Student must be registered student of Andrews University Qualifications Summary FAA Commercial Pilot Certificate with single engine rating. FAA  Flight Instructor Certificate. Hold a current 2nd class medical. FAA Instrument Instructor and Multi-engine Instructor Preferred. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top AIRPARK OPERATIONS - Flight Instructor - Staff Job Classification Hourly Under Half (<20) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2020-02-10 Position Summary Under general direction of the Chief Flight Instructor, conducts quality flight instruction required in the professional pilot programs at Andrews University. Qualifications Summary FAA Commercial Pilot Certificate with single engine rating. FAA  Flight Instructor Certificate. Hold a current 2nd class medical. FAA Instrument Instructor and Multi-engine Instructor Preferred. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top AIRPARK OPERATIONS - Aircraft Mechanic Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-05-07 Position Summary Under general direction of the lead shop mechanic, provide maintenance service at Andrews University. fleet of Piper aircraft. Qualifications Summary Current FAA Aircraft Maintenance Certificate with both the Airframe and Powerplant ratings Inspection Authorization preferred Bachelors’ degree, degree preferred Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top BIOLOGY - Admin Asst School of Life and Molecular Sciences (1.00) Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-31 Position Summary One of a two-person Administrative Assistant team who provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for School Life and Molecular Sciences, and supports the School Chair, program directors, faculty, and students across the Sustainable Agriculture, Biology, and Chemistry & Biochemistry programs in partnership with a second admin. This position coordinates day-to-day administrative functions, welcomes people, supports academic operations and recruiting, assists with student services, manages records and communications, coordinates events and projects, and serves as a key liaison to university offices. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, technologically proficient, outgoing, and manages multiple priorities in a collaborative, cross-disciplinary team. Qualifications Summary Must have a 4-year college degree or equivalent job experience in a dynamic office environment. Must have excellent, multi-modal communication skills. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top CAMPUS SAFETY - Security Officer Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2025-03-17 Position Summary The responsibilities of this position are to fulfill the needs of a Security Officer, capable of working in the Patrol and Dispatch Division. This position is designed to assist in shift coverage and will float between both divisions and all shifts (morning, afternoon, nights). When not on shift coverage, they will mostly work M-F on the afternoon shift. This position is considered an essential employee and will be responsible to work a shift schedule that can include; working during a section of a 24 hour day, working weekends and holidays, including during Sabbath hours. Qualifications Summary This position requires employees who perform well under high-stress situations and have excellent customer service skills. They must be detail oriented and capable of managing their daily tasks with little to no supervision. They must have great communication skills both verbally and in writing. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top CAMPUS SAFETY - Security Officer Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2025-05-05 Position Summary The responsibilities of this position are to fulfill the needs of a Security Officer, capable of working in the Patrol or Dispatch Division. Primary responsibilities will be Patrol and secondary responsibilities will be Dispatch. This position is considered an essential employee and will be responsible to work a shift schedule that can include; working during a section of a 24 hour day, working weekends and holidays, including during Sabbath hours. This posting is for a primary role in Dispatch working an afternoon shift. Qualifications Summary This position requires employees who perform well under high-stress situations and have excellent customer service skills. They must be detail oriented and capable of managing their daily tasks with little to no supervision. They must have great communication skills both verbally and in writing. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top CHEMISTRY - Admin Asst School of Life and Molecular Sciences (0.75) Job Classification Hourly 3/4-time (30-34) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-31 Position Summary One of a two-person Administrative Assistant team who provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for School Life and Molecular Sciences, and supports the School Chair, program directors, faculty, and students across the Sustainable Agriculture, Biology, and Chemistry & Biochemistry programs in partnership with a second admin. This position coordinates day-to-day administrative functions, welcomes people, supports academic operations and recruiting, assists with student services, manages records and communications, coordinates events and projects, and serves as a key liaison to university offices. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, technologically proficient, outgoing, and manages multiple priorities in a collaborative, cross-disciplinary team. Qualifications Summary Must have a 4-year college degree or equivalent job experience in a dynamic office environment. Must have excellent, multi-modal communication skills. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top CHILDRENS LEARNING CENTER - Lead Teacher - Preschool Program Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2027-08-23 Position Summary The Crayon Box Children’s Learning Center is seeking a dependable and energetic Preschool Lead Teacher for our 3-year-old classroom beginning in August 2027. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position for someone passionate about helping young children build a strong foundation for learning through purposeful play, routines, and age-appropriate activities. We’re looking for a confident, organized team player committed to helping children grow spiritually, socially, emotionally, and academically. Schedule: Monday-Friday, 7:30 a.m.- 4:00 p.m., with a one-hour unpaid lunch break. Qualifications Summary Must be at least 19 years old with a high school diploma or GED. Minimum of one year of experience in an early childhood education (ECE) center and must meet the State of Michigan requirements for a Lead Teacher. Dependable and highly punctual, with strong time management, organization, and classroom management skills. Able to effectively manage classroom materials, resources, routines, and responsibilities. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top DEANS OFFICE-COLL OF PROFESSIONS - Program Effectiveness and Process Analyst Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-06-24 Applications Taken Until 2026-07-31 Position Summary The College of Professions at Andrews University seeks an analyst to provide advisory services focused on program effectiveness, system design, governance, and strategy. This role will analyze existing structures and design frameworks, systems, and recommendations to improve academic partnerships, innovation initiatives (including the Adventist Innovation Network), and institutional processes. The role is strictly consultative and does not include operational implementation or administrative duties. Qualifications Summary Experience with academic quality, coordinating compliance with quality standards and implementing corrective actions. Experience in coordinating institutional research. Demonstrated leadership in academic administration through the management of academic operations. Experience in supervising faculty and implementing performance evaluation systems. Experience in evidence-based planning in academic administration. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top DEANS OFFICE-SEMINARY - Grant Writer Job Classification Hourly Under Half (<20) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-02 Position Summary The Grant Writer will support the mission of the Seminary by identifying, developing, and submitting grant proposals to secure funding for academic programs, student support initiatives, ministry training, and institutional development. This is a part-time position (20 hours per week) requiring strong writing skills, attention to detail, and alignment with the Seminary’s faith-based mission. Qualifications Summary Bachelors degree required (Masters preferred in nonprofit administration, theology, or related field) Proven experience in grant writing, fundraising, or nonprofit development Strong written communication and storytelling skills Ability to work independently and manage multiple deadlines Familiarity with faith-based organizations preferred High level of organization and attention to detail Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top DEVELOPMENT - Gift Records Associate Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-06-03 Applications Taken Until 2026-09-04 Position Summary The Gift Records Associate processes all pledges and donations received by the University and maintains the integrity of the donor financial records of the University. Processing tasks include receiving, recording, receipting, acknowledging, depositing funds, and maintaining critical gift accounting records. The unique skills that are required of the Gift Associate help to ensure the integrity of the gift-related financial data of the University.  The Gift Records Associate reports to the Director of Development. Qualifications Summary The Gift Records Associate must be extremely organized and detail oriented so that donor intent is met regarding allocation, amount, and degree of anonymity, and that all gifts are documented completely, correctly, in a timely manner and are ready for entry into the Andrews University Banner system.  The Gift Records Administrator will work as part of a team to engage in strategic and purposeful use of the database system to strengthen development practices. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top ELEMENTARY SCHOOL - Substitute Teacher - RMES Job Classification Hourly Under Half (<20) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-25 Applications Taken Until 2026-12-30 Position Summary Manages student learning in accordance with the goals and directives of the classroom teacher and school. Qualifications Summary Must be able to follow oral and written directions and have the ability to establish effective working relationships with staff and students. Ability to maintain effective classroom management strategies. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top ENGLISH - Administrative Assistant -- School of Creative Arts and Humanities Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-01 Position Summary The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the School of Creative Arts and Humanities, serving the School Chair, program directors, faculty, and students across the English, History/Political Science, and Visual Arts, Communication & Design (VACD) programs. This position coordinates the day-to-day administrative functions of the school, supports academic operations, assists with student services, manages records and communications, coordinates events and projects, and serves as a key liaison between the school and university offices. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, detail-oriented, technologically proficient, and able to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative academic environment. Qualifications Summary The ideal candidate is a highly organized, detail-oriented professional with strong administrative, organizational, and communication skills. The successful candidate exercises sound judgment and discretion, manages multiple priorities with initiative, and works effectively in a collaborative academic environment. Proficiency with office technology, the ability to learn university systems, and experience coordinating complex administrative processes are preferred. Prior higher education experience is desirable. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top FINANCIAL ADMIN VP - Accounts Payable/Expense Management Supervisor Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2026-08-01 Applications Taken Until 2026-08-10 Position Summary Supervision of University Accounts payable. Responsible for Corporate Card Administration. \"Help Desk\" for Emburse software program. Monitors corporate card reporting. Works with Accountant responsible for Emburse Software User interface to improve and optimize use of Travel and Expense Software. Assist with general departmental office duties. Qualifications Summary Enjoys working with and mentoring student employees. Must be able avialable to work in the office most days during normal business hours. Proficient with Excel. Detail oriented. Organized. Able to deal with disruption and regain focus quickly. Good customer services skills. Comfortable learning new software. Works will with others. Team player. Excellent communication skills. Prefered familiarity with Accounting and/or basic business processes and practices. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Must be a Seventh-day Adventist in good and regular standing. Full Position Description Apply on-line >> Back to top GROUNDS - Groundskeeper-Mechanical Job Classification Hourly Full-time (35-40) Wages Commensurate with experience Date Available 2025-08-14 Position Summary Performs a variety of duties in the development and maintenance of the Arboretum and Grounds. Operates and assists in the maintenance of Grounds equipment. Responsibilities include: the maintenance and general beautification of Andrews University Groun"
